==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Attack Battalion Convoys''' at level 10.

Evolves into '''Hyper Battalion Convoys''' at level 30 using [[Catfruit]] and XP.

==Strategy/Usage==
This unit is designed to rush to the frontline as fast as possible and hold the line. It is particularly effective against enemies that apply knockback, against whom other tanks and meatshields may struggle, but this vehicle will rush back in immediately, not to mention how it will get more chances to reposition if the frontline moves, as it stands still after attacking otherwise. Enemies with Knockback also give this unit more chances to [[Weaken]] its targets, further enhancing its defensive capabilities. [[Super Metal Hippoe]] is an especially good match due to its virtually nonexistent damage against this anti-Metal tank. For Zombies and Reds, it also has great matchups, but will face competition from [[Sushi Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Sushi Cat]] against Reds, who is more spammable and equally capable of weakening, and struggle in some zombie stages, as [[Soulstrike]] may cause it to needlessly get stuck on a dead Zombie while the army advances unprotected.

Although this unit works similarly to [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut]] and [[Express Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Maglev]], it should not be used for damage, as its DPS leaves a lot to be desired.

==='''True Form'''===
Hyper Battalion Convoys gains a huge HP and speed increase, which on its own makes this True Form worth getting if you were already using this unit. However, it also receives a massive forward piercing range buff through a guaranteed level 3 [[Wave Attack]], which brings its utility up by a lot. While its effective range with [[Omni Strike]] is already decently high, this Wave Attack makes it even higher while also doubling its DPH in the process.

To compliment this, Hyper Battalion Convoys's knockback count was doubled from 2 to 4. This generally allows it to get more attacks in before dying, without it needing to rely on enemies with Knockback. It also gains the ability to [[Knockback]] enemies, which doesn't do much on its own, but can help in gaining ground (although it is worth keeping in mind that the Knockback does cause it to miss its Wave Attack for enemies struck by its Omni Strike). Overall, these changes improve what it does considerably.

